---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What this site does and does not collect. Images are processed entirely in your browser and are never uploaded to any server."
  h1="Privacy policy"
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  blurb="The short version: your images never leave your device, and there is no account system, so there is very little about you for us to hold."
  updated="2026-08-07"
>
  <h2>The images you process</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool on {SITE.name} runs inside your web browser using WebAssembly and the browser's
    own image APIs. When you drop a file onto a tool, that file is read into your browser's
    memory on your own computer or phone. It is never transmitted to us or to anyone else.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is not a policy promise that you have to take on trust — it is a property of how the
    site is built, and you can verify it. Load any tool page, disconnect from the internet, and
    then process an image. It works, because there is nothing on the other end of a connection
    to talk to. You can also open your browser's developer tools, watch the Network tab, and
    confirm that processing a file produces no outbound requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because we never receive your files, there is no server-side copy to delete, no retention
    period to describe, and no risk of a data breach exposing your photographs.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do collect</h2>

  <h3>Hosting logs</h3>
  <p>
    This site is served by a hosting provider that keeps standard web server logs. These
    typically record your IP address, the page requested, the time, your browser's user agent
    string and the referring page. This happens for every website you visit and is used for
    security and to keep the service running. We do not combine these logs with anything else
    or use them to build a profile of you.
  </p>

  <h3>Settings stored in your browser</h3>
  <p>
    Some tools remember your last-used settings — a quality level, a preferred output format —
    so you do not have to set them again on your next visit. These are stored in your browser's
    local storage on your own device. They contain no personal information, they are never sent
    anywhere, and clearing your browser data removes them.
  </p>

  <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, usernames or passwords, because there is no login.</li>
    <li>No email addresses, unless you choose to write to us.</li>
    <li>No payment details, because nothing here is for sale.</li>
    <li>No copies of your images, thumbnails, or metadata extracted from them.</li>
    <li>No cross-site tracking of your browsing elsewhere.</li>
  </ul>

  {
    SITE.analytics.plausibleDomain && (
      <Fragment>
        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Plausible Analytics to count page views and see which tools are being used.
          Plausible does not use cookies, does not collect personal data, and does not track
          people across websites or over time. It reports aggregate numbers only.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    )
  }

  {
    SITE.adsense.enabled && (
      <Fragment>
        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          This site displays advertisements supplied by Google AdSense, which is how it is paid
          for. Advertising involves third parties, so this section matters.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies to serve ads on this site. The
            DoubleClick cookie enables Google and its partners to serve ads based on your visits
            here and to other sites on the internet.
          </li>
          <li>
            Third-party vendors and ad networks may also use cookies or similar technologies to
            serve and measure advertising.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting{' '}
            <a
              href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads"
              rel="noopener nofollow"
              target="_blank"
            >
              Google's Ads Settings
            </a>
            . You can also opt out of third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalised
            advertising at{' '}
            <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">
              aboutads.info
            </a>
            .
          </li>
          <li>
            If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, you will
            be shown a consent message before any advertising cookies are set, and you can change
            your choice at any time.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Advertising is kept away from the tool controls and download buttons deliberately, so
          that you never click an advertisement when you meant to click a button.
        </p>
        <p>
          Advertisers never receive your images. Advertising code has no access to the files you
          process, which are handled entirely in a separate part of the page.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    )
  }

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages link to platform documentation, such as Google's guidance on thumbnail sizes or a
    marketplace's image requirements. Those sites have their own privacy policies, which we do
    not control.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children and we do not knowingly collect information from
    anyone. Since there is no account system and no data submission of any kind, there is
    nothing for a child to submit.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Data protection law in the UK, the EU and elsewhere gives you rights over personal data held
    about you, including the right to request access to it or its deletion. Because we hold no
    personal data beyond standard server logs, in most cases there is nothing to disclose or
    erase. If you want to make a request anyway, write to us and we will respond.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in a way that affects you — most likely because advertising or
    analytics has been added — the date at the top of this page will change. Substantive changes
    will be described here rather than quietly folded in.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, or
    through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
